{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":39312,\"title\":\"Restrepo\",\"tagline\":\"One platoon, one valley, one year\",\"overview\":\"Directors Hetherington and Junger spend a year with the 2nd Battalion of the United States Army located in one of Afghanistan's most dangerous valleys. The documentary provides insight and empathy on how to win the battle through hard work, deadly gunfights and mutual friendships while the unit must push back the Taliban.\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/62DCMBMJU1ZVezVEawyatpFoJwI.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/9G38qGg7T0qIjfl5OxyQnypB9Y4.jpg\",\"rating\":7.2,\"voteCount\":384,\"year\":2010,\"runtime\":93,\"genres\":[\"War\",\"Documentary\"],\"status\":\"Released\",\"type\":\"movie\",\"countries\":[{\"code\":\"US\",\"name\":\"United States of America\"}],\"budget\":0,\"revenue\":1437000,\"director\":\"Tim Hetherington\",\"cast\":[{\"id\":131948,\"name\":\"Tim Hetherington\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qRBQv3Tqg5btMwBFGkr8m1n4jmS.jpg\"},{\"id\":21863,\"name\":\"Sebastian Junger\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/lxQIfHbKXX6rPKwKb8QjyyIKqMc.jpg\"},{\"id\":550839,\"name\":\"Juan \\\"Doc\\\" Restrepo\",\"character\":\"Himself\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":550840,\"name\":\"Dan Kearney\",\"character\":\"Himself\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":550841,\"name\":\"LaMonta Caldwell\",\"character\":\"Himself\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":550842,\"name\":\"Aron Hijar\",\"character\":\"Himself\",\"photo\":null}],\"similar\":[{\"id\":1058616,\"title\":\"20 Days in Mariupol\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zIRp1IeuPh4GgqFCH3y0DQuY9xP.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/986n9SAXsuxpPJzFAWK3azPknX0.jpg\",\"rating\":8.1,\"year\":2023,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"As the Russian invasion begins, a team of Ukrainian journalists trapped in the besieged city of Mariupol struggle to continue their work documenting the war's atrocities.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":8885,\"title\":\"Waltz with Bashir\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zQaCv7lKwHsh0YSHkt1QNjIOZ1c.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/cMoiIk3tD6qshxccYRjjym7l5YV.jpg\",\"rating\":7.7,\"year\":2008,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"A film director from Israel interviews fellow veterans of the 1982 invasion of Lebanon to reconstruct his own memories of his term of service in that conflict.\",\"genres\":[\"Animation\",\"Documentary\",\"Drama\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":543580,\"title\":\"They Shall Not Grow Old\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yMGfJeTXUdIjOqjS0jJfjgYEuYC.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/94PXfCDB6TrTx1YwuUjzIpVXT2i.jpg\",\"rating\":7.8,\"year\":2018,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"A documentary about World War I with never-before-seen footage to commemorate the centennial of Armistice Day, and the end of the war.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"History\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":576017,\"title\":\"For Sama\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mDna51F8QfrJFZOgPGQUz3VKqsB.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/hiqB5fFZ230MeFAGLPahoy06UOE.jpg\",\"rating\":8.2,\"year\":2019,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"A love letter from a young mother to her daughter, the film tells the story of Waad al-Kateab’s life through five years of the uprising in Aleppo, Syria as she falls in love, gets married and gives birth to Sama, all while cataclysmic conflict rises around her.  Her camera captures incredible stories of loss, laughter and survival as Waad wrestles with an impossible choice– whether or not to flee the city to protect her daughter’s life, when leaving means abandoning the struggle for freedom for which she has already sacrificed so much.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":263614,\"title\":\"Virunga\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7ULqkiqpxWfQxNHRq5PeZjJQ3f6.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/6KDpjoCxlNapSzqUdagloiQqljh.jpg\",\"rating\":7.9,\"year\":2014,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Virunga in the Democratic Republic of the Congo is Africa's oldest national park, a UNESCO world heritage site, and a contested ground among insurgencies seeking to topple the government that see untold profits in the land. Among this ongoing power struggle, Virunga also happens to be the last natural habitat for the critically endangered mountain gorilla. The only thing standing in the way of the forces closing in around the gorillas: a handful of passionate park rangers and journalists fighting to secure the park's borders and expose the corruption of its enemies. Filled with shocking footage, and anchored by the surprisingly deep and gentle characters of the gorillas themselves, Virunga is a galvanizing call to action around an ongoing political and environmental crisis in the Congo.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":37828,\"title\":\"Armadillo\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/aezjTpjt0sdQV9X8XiSH2oHWEt7.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/eje6RaOBEPlPuiuX4TDwug8XXDd.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"year\":2010,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Danish soldiers are sent to Afghanistan in 2009 for 6 months, to help stabilize the country against the Taliban. They're stationed on Armadillo military base in Helman province. Unlike other war movies, this is the real deal – no actors.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":13180,\"title\":\"Zeitgeist: Addendum\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/5zlBxoyWRyzPOHO7QmmAC1WG9bK.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/usAD0Fwx7pInwJtHwKiJnssp4iZ.jpg\",\"rating\":7.2,\"year\":2008,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Director Peter Joseph examines examples of economic subjugation and offers solutions based on alignment with nature.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"History\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":127918,\"title\":\"The Gatekeepers\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/y7B7Ko7ZEXKcBLkO8HiGFAxAKjA.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/7ZbfWHkSZMiRmmFwxUpVcgMWFEO.jpg\",\"rating\":6.9,\"year\":2012,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"In an unprecedented and candid series of interviews, six former heads of the Shin Bet — Israel's intelligence and security agency — speak about their role in Israel's decades-long counterterrorism campaign, discussing their controversial methods and whether the ends ultimately justify the means.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"History\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":84170,\"title\":\"Five Broken Cameras\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/xPNfzTzvjbcpMUTaGxnk15njMg3.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/2DgKCfO49b8KwF18bWPS1Efpjpt.jpg\",\"rating\":7.5,\"year\":2011,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Five broken cameras – and each one has a powerful tale to tell. Embedded in the bullet-ridden remains of digital technology is the story of Emad Burnat, a farmer from the Palestinian village of Bil’in, which famously chose nonviolent resistance when the Israeli army encroached upon its land to make room for Jewish colonists. Emad buys his first camera in 2005 to document the birth of his fourth son, Gibreel. Over the course of the film, he becomes the peaceful archivist of an escalating struggle as olive trees are bulldozed, lives are lost, and a wall is built to segregate burgeoning Israeli settlements.\",\"genres\":[\"War\",\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":84288,\"title\":\"The Invisible War\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ph9Lo3pMNmTXFQa9wZVdCKL2tRe.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/zKBY36XNmc9ehJwPVQWvQ4fi1B.jpg\",\"rating\":7.1,\"year\":2012,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"An investigative and powerfully emotional documentary about the epidemic of rape of soldiers within the US military, the institutions that perpetuate and cover up its existence, and its profound personal and social consequences.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"War\",\"Crime\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":416211,\"title\":\"The White Helmets\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/w5wJW2MrmhoZYSrCzaB8WxkYDEC.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/hkbzt4YyjrduGqeN9kHEdXMCEQm.jpg\",\"rating\":7.4,\"year\":2016,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"As daily airstrikes pound civilian targets in Syria, a group of indomitable first responders risk their lives to rescue victims from the rubble.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\",\"War\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":272288,\"title\":\"Afghanistan's Opium Trail\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/2hHSAAIB8ixnU2jZmt5M3zotdUU.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/1cMvDn5Czqw3KvbJDsWCVtunLk8.jpg\",\"rating\":7.5,\"year\":2007,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Over 90% of the world's opium now comes from Afghanistan. In this shocking new film, we ride the drugs caravan, from cultivation, to process, to market. On route, we lift the curtain on the hidden world of the drug barons; learn how to process heroin in the crudest of laboratories and encounter deadly gunfights on the Iranian border.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null}],\"videos\":[{\"key\":\"-DjqR6OucBc\",\"name\":\"\\\"Restrepo\\\" Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"daysUntil\":null}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}